{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792505342,"nonce":"5mhRGRnwfMithArVdN6AXwS3wAM=","message":"Initial controls before implementation fail both producer cases: foreground projection loses the image, and image-only motion batch is empty because RGBA was written to the static late-image list. Both offscreen controls fail: static image-only foreground group leaves blue instead of half green, and a red image covers a later green foreground shape. Logs: /private/tmp/blinc-fgrgba-negative-cpu.log and /private/tmp/blinc-fgrgba-negative-gpu.log.\n\nForeground raw RGBA now uses foreground_dynamic_images in the active batch and captures local foreground primitive/path/command cursors. It retains explicit and unrepresented ancestor opacity, leaving represented foreground group opacity to ordered composition. Foreground projection, move, merge, clear, content predicates and static-cache deferral retain images. Existing foreground cache guards now include image-only streams. Composite scratch still collapses emission into its existing background stream. No primitive/shader ABI changes.\n\nExpanded controls found the separate-layer public render_tree path did not dispatch explicit foreground streams. Its first post-producer-fix image-only frame was blue instead of half green (/private/tmp/blinc-fgrgba-simple-negative.log). It now takes foreground from each separate context and dispatches those whole streams once after the layer passes, preserving shape/path/aux data when images disappear. Tests cover image -\u003e changed pixels -\u003e shapes -\u003e empty across all three application routes with and without a glass node.\n\nFive final normal-mode GPU cases pass so far, including static/canvas/motion image-only dispatch; image vs later shape order; nested image groups, nonzero rectangular/empty clips, true path tail, projected 4x MSAA and public glass preserve/clear hand-offs; explicit supplied-sequence and no-cursor legacy image API; and a deterministic static canvas kept inside a foreground motion group through opacity 1 -\u003e 0.5 -\u003e 0 -\u003e 0.75 -\u003e 1. The deterministic fixture keeps its images in the motion stream rather than the separate dynamic-canvas band. Cross-stream ancestor isolation remains outside this slice, as do shaped clips, affine mapping, separate text/SVG/ImageElement and named Sample. Foreground motion retains the existing full-paint fallback. Capability sweep and full gate are pending.","files":null}]}